  56:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h **** 
  57:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     The functions in this header are meant as convenience functions where
  58:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     actual time values can be specified as a delay time,
  59:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     rather than a number of cycles to wait for.
  60:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h **** 
  61:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     This requires that the clock frequency of the device is provided
  62:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     in the \c #F_CPU macro in units of Hertz.  The macro must be defined
  63:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     before including the <util/delay.h> header.  It can be defined
  64:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     in the source code like indicated above, or it can be defined on the
  65:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     command line / in a Makefile by means of <tt>-D F_CPU=...</tt>
  66:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h **** 
