  70:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     <a href="https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc/AVR-Built-in-Functions.html#index-_005f_005fbuiltin
  71:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     >__builtin_avr_delay_cycles()</a> is used instead.
  72:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h **** 
  73:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     In any case, the delay functions provided by this header will not disable
  74:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     interrupts, which means hat the delay time will be longer than
  75:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     specified when interrupts occur while a delay function is running.
  76:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h **** 
  77:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     In order for these functions to work as intended, compiler
  78:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     optimizations <em>must</em> be enabled, and the delay time
  79:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     <em>must</em> be an expression that is a known constant at
  80:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     compile time.  If these requirements are not met, the resulting
  81:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     delay will be much longer (and basically unpredictable), and
  82:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     applications that otherwise do not use floating-point calculations
  83:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     will experience severe code bloat by the floating-point library
  84:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     routines linked into the application.
  85:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     The idea is
  86:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     that compile-time constant expressions will be eliminated by
  87:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     compiler optimization so floating-point expressions can be used
  88:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     to calculate the number of delay cycles needed based on the CPU
  89:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     frequency passed by the macro F_CPU.
  90:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h **** 
  91:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     The functions available allow the specification of microsecond, and
  92:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     millisecond delays directly, using the application-supplied macro
  93:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     F_CPU as the CPU clock frequency in Hertz.
  94:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h **** */
