 100:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h **** /** \ingroup util_delay
 101:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     \def F_CPU
 102:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     \brief CPU frequency in Hz
 103:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h **** 
 104:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     The macro F_CPU specifies the CPU frequency in Hertz to be considered by
 105:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     the delay functions.  This macro is normally supplied by the
 106:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     environment (e.g. from within a project header, or the project's
 107:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     Makefile).  The value 1 MHz here is only provided as a
 108:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     fallback default if no such user-provided definition could be found.
 109:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h **** 
 110:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     In terms of the delay functions, the CPU frequency can be given as
 111:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****     a floating-point constant (e.g. 3.6864e6 for 3.6864 MHz).
