 121:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h **** 
 122:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h **** /**
 123:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    \ingroup util_delay
 124:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h **** 
 125:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    Perform a delay of \c __ms milliseconds.
 126:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h **** 
 127:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    The macro #F_CPU is supposed to be defined to a
 128:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    constant defining the CPU clock frequency in Hertz.
 129:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h **** 
 130:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h **** -  If \c __builtin_avr_delay_cycles() is
 131:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h **** \if GIT_BRANCH_IS_ONLINEDOCS
 132:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    supported
 133:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h **** \else
 134:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    \ref faq_toolchain_support "supported"
 135:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h **** \endif
 136:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    by the compiler, then
 137:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    the maximal possible delay is 4294967.04 / f<sub>CPU</sub> milliseconds
 138:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    where f<sub>CPU</sub> denotes the CPU frequency in units of 1 MHz.
 139:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    This is around 71 minutes / f<sub>CPU</sub>.
 140:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    Values greater than that are saturated to this value.
 141:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h **** 
 142:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h **** -  Otherwise, _delay_loop_2() is used as a fallback, and the maximal
 143:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    possible delay is 262.14 / f<sub>CPU</sub> milliseconds.
 144:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    When the user requests a delay which exceeds the maximum possible one,
 145:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    _delay_ms() provides a decreased resolution functionality. In this
 146:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    mode _delay_ms() will work with a resolution of 1/10&nbsp;ms, providing
 147:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    delays up to 6.5535 seconds (independent from CPU frequency).  The
 148:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    user will not be informed about decreased resolution.
 149:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h **** .
 150:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h **** 
 151:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    Conversion of \c __ms into clock cycles may not always result in
 152:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    an integral value.  By default, the clock cycles are rounded up to the next
 153:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    integer. This ensures that the user gets at least \c __ms
 154:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    microseconds of delay.
 155:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    Alternatively, by defining the macro \c __DELAY_ROUND_DOWN__, or
 156:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    \c __DELAY_ROUND_CLOSEST__, before including this header file, the
 157:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    algorithm can be made to round down, or round to closest integer,
 158:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    respectively.
 159:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h **** 
 160:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    \note The implementation of _delay_ms() based on
 161:C:/Users/mohdn/avr-libc-cmake/avr-libc/include/util\delay.h ****    \c __builtin_avr_delay_cycles() is not backward compatible with older
